<title>USA: Level One sets 3-for-2 stock split.</title>
<headline>Level One sets 3-for-2 stock split.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Level One Communications Inc Tuesday said it will split its stock on a three-for-two basis, payable August 26 to shareholders of record on August 5.</p>
<p>Following the split, the number of shares outstanding will increase to roughly 20.2 million from the current 13.5 million.</p>
<p>&quot;The 3-for-2 stock split reflects our confidence in our business model and our desire to enhance the liquidity of trading in our shares,&quot; Robert Pepper, chief executive officer, said in a statement.</p>
</text>
